<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piri Mehmed Pasha (Ramadanid)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ramazanoğlu Piri Mehmed Pasha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piri Mehmed Pasha was a 16th-century ruler of the Ramadanid family, the Turkmen dynasty that governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adana">Adana</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> as hereditary Ottoman governors after 1517. He is remembered chiefly as a builder: he completed the Great Mosque complex of Adana begun by his predecessor, one of the main monuments of Ramadanid rule.</p></div>
